  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "i22",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Typing: the help popups come up far too fast",
      "excerpt": "Typing: the help popups come up far too fast",
      "text": "Want a standard popup delay, I think someone else is working on that.  This might be a user setting.  Check",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-20T00:52:47.369Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-20T00:53:33.739Z",
          "html": "<p>Checked.  The code panes already wait the standard delay, 800ms, but they don't read it from the setting.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>The standard delay is Spell UI's <code>--ui-hover-delay</code> (800ms), a style setting under Motion.  Tooltips wait it too (<code>--ui-tooltip-delay</code>, by default the same).</li>\n  <li>The other work you remembered was epic-engine's T105 (r80):  the rule that tooltips use Spell UI's tooltip with the standard delay.  It's done, and it's about tooltips, not the code panes.</li>\n  <li>The code panes' hovers, suggestion list and signature help use their own copy of 800ms (<code title=\"app/src/app/ui/codePopups.ts\">HOVER_DELAY</code>).  So changing the setting wouldn't reach them.</li>\n  <li>There's no setting for it in the editor's Settings… dialog.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Proposed:  the code panes read <code>--ui-hover-delay</code> from the page when a popup waits, so one setting changes every popup.  Adding it to Settings… is a separate call:  say if you want that too.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-20T00:53:07.720Z"
      }
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
